  "body": "\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nWhen attempting to join `#!:http://matrix.org` (exactly as written), eg. after a botched copy-paste from something that auto-inserts `http://`, this results in a 500 M_UNKNOWN error rather than a validation error like I would expect.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n- Go to 'explore public rooms'\r\n- Enter `#!:http://matrix.org`\r\n- Click 'join'\r\n\r\n### Version information\r\n\r\n- **Homeserver**: pixie.town\r\n\r\nIf not matrix.org:\r\n\r\n- **Version**: Synapse 1.21.0\r\n\r\n- **Install method**: Unknown, not my Synapse\r\n\r\n- **Platform**: Unknown, not my Synapse\r\n",
